<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
    <IsAotCompatible>false</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Bytes captured off a real wire, shared by every test suite that parses that wire, and NOTHING
    else. Deliberately carries zero PackageReference.

    Why this is not a folder inside Verbara.Sdk.TestInfrastructure: that project carries
    Testcontainers, so referencing it from a unit-test suite would hand that suite the whole Docker
    client graph to read nineteen bytes. Verbara.Sdk.TestInfrastructure.Http already exists for
    exactly this reason and its csproj records what the alternative cost — WireMock's transitive
    graph landing in suites that did not need it dropped measured line coverage from 80.42% to
    61.96% while every test still passed (ADR-0041 D7). The same confinement rule, applied one
    project earlier.

    Why this is not a per-suite copy of the bytes: a captured fixture exists to stop a parser being
    held to its own encoder. Two copies of the capture can drift apart exactly like two parsers did,
    which is the failure this project is here to make impossible.
  -->

</Project>
